+  // Mitcad (mitcad#2384): how near its boundary an end of the line must lie
+  // to be put on it, in each parameter of each surface: aTol, and for a
+  // range longer than a full turn (2 pi) as much more as the range is
+  // longer, so that a surface parametrized by arc length (a range of
+  // hundreds) is given the room a surface of the same shape parametrized by
+  // angle or over [0, 1] is. aTol is a thousandth of a parameter, which on
+  // an arc-length parametrized loft's side was a micrometre: the section of
+  // that side with its mirror image, where the two share their tangent
+  // plane at the top boundary, stopped 4 micrometres below it (5e-3 in v
+  // over a range of 387) and was not put on it, while the same loft
+  // parametrized over [0, 1] in v (the kernel's own) was. SeekPointOnBoundary
+  // still finds the point on the boundary where the surfaces meet, within
+  // its own tolerance, or adds none.
+  const auto aTolOf = [aTol](const double theRange) {
+    constexpr double aFullTurn = 2.0 * M_PI;
+    return theRange > aFullTurn ? aTol * theRange / aFullTurn : aTol;
+  };
